<section class="section section--ink" aria-labelledby="s5-title">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="process">
      <div class="process__aside">
        <h2 class="process__title" id="s5-title">Our Post-Quantum Cryptography Assessment Process</h2>
        <p class="process__lede">Every engagement moves from discovery to a plan your teams can execute. We work with your engineers and vendors so the roadmap reflects how your systems are really built and released.</p>
      </div>

      <ol class="process__list" data-process>
        <li class="step">
          <span class="step__marker" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <h3 class="step__title">Scope and Business Context</h3>
          <p class="step__text">We start with what you need to protect: critical systems, regulated data, how long information must stay confidential and the obligations that shape your timeline.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="step">
          <span class="step__marker" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <h3 class="step__title">Cryptographic Discovery and Inventory</h3>
          <p class="step__text">Using configuration review, code and certificate analysis, interviews and available scanning data, we build an inventory of algorithms, keys, certificates and libraries across your environment.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="step">
          <span class="step__marker" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <h3 class="step__title">Quantum Risk Assessment and Prioritization</h3>
          <p class="step__text">Each asset is ranked by quantum exposure, data sensitivity and confidentiality lifetime, producing a risk register that shows what to change first.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="step">
          <span class="step__marker" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <h3 class="step__title">Crypto-Agility and Dependency Review</h3>
          <p class="step__text">We examine how easily each system can adopt new algorithms and identify blockers such as hard-coded cryptography, legacy protocols, constrained devices and vendor dependencies.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="step">
